    <briefdescription>
<para>Manages atomic project state transitions with an append-only audit trail. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>State transitions are validated against the allowed transition table before being committed. Both the new state record and the audit-log entry are written in a single RocksDB write batch to ensure atomicity.</para>
<para>RocksDB key layout ────────────────── lifecycle:&lt;project_id&gt; → current <ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1projects_1a83a8895d15c04fb2fd197304c0873e44" kindref="member">ProjectState</ref> (string) lifecycle_log:&lt;project_id&gt;:&lt;ts_ns&gt; → <ref refid="structthemis_1_1projects_1_1_project_state_transition" kindref="compound">ProjectStateTransition</ref> JSON</para>
<para>All methods are thread-safe (protected by an internal shared_mutex). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
